<title>FINLAND: ASPO SEES 1997 SALES, EARNINGS UP ON 1996.</title>
<headline>ASPO SEES 1997 SALES, EARNINGS UP ON 1996.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish engineering group Aspoyhtyma Oy said in a statement on Tuesday it expected turnover to rise and earnings to improve in 1997 compared to last year.  </p>
<p>&quot;The group's net sales and profits are expected to improve during 1997,&quot; Aspoyhtyma said.</p>
<p>Last year, Aspo's turnover at 1.11 billion markka was slightly higher than in 1995 while group profit before extraordinary items and taxes fell 34 percent to 65 million markka.</p>
<p>Aspo said it will release its full financial statement for 1996 on February 27.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 9 - 680 50 245</p>
